# Working in this project

Use the mise tasks in `mise.toml` when you work in this project. Never call a tool directly when a mise task exists for it. Check your work with `mise run check` before you commit.
[[- if eq .backend "ts" ]]

## TypeScript

The backend is in `backend/`. Run its tasks from that directory: `mise run dev`, `mise run test`, `mise run lint`, `mise run build` and `mise run openapi`.

Vite+ is the toolchain. Its CLI is `vp`, and it installs Node and pnpm.

- Call `vp` directly only for a command that has no mise task, such as `vp install` or `vp add <package>`. Running a tool through its mise task loads `.env`.
- Never call `vite`, `vitest`, `oxlint` or `oxfmt` directly.
- Import test functions from `vite-plus/test`.
- Relative imports end in `.ts`, because Node runs the source files directly in development.
- After changing a route, run `mise run openapi` and commit `openapi.json`.
[[- end ]]
